     "id": "clm_surfrad_bare_step3_p1",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the bare-patch SurfaceRadiation partition against clm_surfrad.csv (step 3, patch 1): a bare patch (ptype = 0, sabv = parveg = 0 on every traced row) with the incident radiation of the step-3 row and the ground/soil albedos of clm_surfalbedo.csv step 2 (SurfaceRadiation runs before the doalb call of its step - clm_driver.F90:658 vs :1325-1364 - so step s uses the albedo computed at step s-1's doalb). Then sabg = forc_solad_vis*(1-albgrd_vis) + forc_solai_vis*(1-albgri_vis) + forc_solad_nir*(1-albgrd_nir) + forc_solai_nir*(1-albgri_nir) = 64.1493509908771570 W/m2, sabg_soil = 318.225002092635634 W/m2, fsa = sabv + sabg = sabg, fsr = albgrd_vis*forc_solad_vis + albgri_vis*forc_solai_vis + albgrd_nir*forc_solad_nir + albgri_nir*forc_solai_nir = 365.768237676828392 W/m2 (all matching the dumped values to round-off), sabg_snow = sabg because frac_sno_albedo = 1 makes albsnd_hst = albsnd = albgrd (SurfaceAlbedoMod.F90:816 with frac_sno_albedo = 1; the W3 albsnd/albsni columns of the clm_surfalbedo.csv step-2 row equal albgrd/albgri bit-exactly, and the dumped sabg_snow equals sabg on all 192 rows), and sabv = parveg = 0 (dumped exactly).",
